        "original_id": "21c7a449-e49a-5bc2-8b3d-0219b82f157c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Arundel Castle, Sussex, Norfolk, England\n- People: Duke of Norfolk\n- Events: English Civil War\n- Concepts: Parliamentarians, Royalists, government of England\n\nFacts:\n- The English Civil War took place from 1642 to 1651.\n- The English Civil War was a series of armed conflicts and political machinations between Parliamentarians, also called Roundheads, and Royalists, also called Cavaliers, mainly over the manner of England's government.\n- Arundel Castle was damaged during the English Civil War.\n- Arundel Castle was restored in the 18th and 19th centuries.\n- Arundel Castle in Sussex is the seat of the Duke of Norfolk.\n- The title Duke of Norfolk refers to the county of Norfolk.",
